<title>GERMANY: Opel chief sees light improvement in car market.</title>
<headline>Opel chief sees light improvement in car market.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>David Herman, the chairman of Adam Opel AG expects only moderate growth in automobile demand 1997, the Leipziger Volkszeitung newspaper reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Herman said the car market will not enjoy a big lift this year because consumption and export trends will likely not strongly improve.</p>
<p>&quot;Presently, we see too many burdens weighing on consumer's decisions to purchase big price-tag products,&quot; Herman told the newspaper.</p>
<p>Opel is the German unit of General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
